  "question": {
    "text": "Let for some function $\\mathrm{y}=f(x), \\int_0^x t f(t) d t=x^2 f(x), x\\gt0$ and $f(2)=3$. Then $f(6)$ is equal to",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "Djg4I",
      "text": "1",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "CdHu4",
      "text": "3",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "SQsTG",
      "text": "6",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "jKnjQ",
      "text": "2",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\begin{aligned} & \\int_0^x t f(t) d t=x^2 f(x) \\\\ & \\Rightarrow \\quad x f(x)=2 x f(x)+x^2 f^{\\prime}(x) \\\\ & \\Rightarrow x^2 \\cdot f^{\\prime}(x)=-x f(x) \\\\ & \\Rightarrow \\quad \\frac{f^{\\prime}(x)}{f(x)}=-\\frac{1}{x} \\\\ & \\\\ & \\quad \\int \\frac{f^{\\prime}(x)}{f(x) d x}=-\\int \\frac{1}{x} d x \\\\ & \\Rightarrow \\quad \\ln f(x)=-\\ln x+C \\\\ & \\\\ & \\quad f(2)=3 \\Rightarrow \\ln 3=-\\ln 2+C \\\\ & \\quad C=\\ln 6 \\\\ & \\Rightarrow \\quad f(x)=\\frac{6}{x} \\Rightarrow f(6)=1\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
